# rpmlint filters of slideshow-lock. Use it with:
#   rpmlint --rpmlintrc packaging/fedora/slideshow-lock.rpmlintrc slideshow-lock.spec <the .src.rpm> <the .noarch.rpm>
#
# libadwaita is not a library that rpm can find by itself: the program loads the typelib Adw-1 (a
# file of the package libadwaita) through PyGObject, gi.require_version("Adw", "1"). No repository of
# Fedora 43/44, CentOS Stream 10 or EPEL 10 has a typelib(...) provide that could be required instead
# (spec, "Requires: libadwaita"), so the package name is the only way to depend on it. rpmlint
# (TagsCheck) only looks at the name: a Requires that starts with "lib" is an explicit-lib-dependency.
addFilter(r"explicit-lib-dependency libadwaita$")
